# DP-119: HTTPS in front of the DEV admin console, https://admin.localhost:3114.
#
# The admin console signs in with Secure, __Host- cookies. Chrome and Firefox treat
# http://localhost as secure, Safari does not: over plain http it drops those cookies and the
# sign-in cannot finish. This proxy gives DEV a real https origin, so cookie security stays the
# same in every environment (never relaxed for development).
#
# - Certificates come from Caddy's own local CA ("Caddy Local Authority"), kept in the DEV volume
#   tls-ca-dev so the root stays the same across restarts. Trusting that root on the Mac is the
#   owner's step: `infra/docker/stack.sh dev tls-ca` exports it and prints the command.
# - DEV only: production terminates TLS at its own edge. No access log (the token of a link is in
#   the fragment and never reaches a server anyway), no admin endpoint, no automatic trust install.
{
	admin off
	skip_install_trust
	local_certs
	auto_https disable_redirects
}

https://admin.localhost, https://localhost {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy admin:3000
}
